NAME
       vgrename - rename a volume group

SYNOPSIS
       vgrename OLD-NAME NEW-NAME

DESCRIPTION
       vgrename gives a volume group a new name. Its LV device paths change
       with it (/dev/OLD/lv becomes /dev/NEW/lv), so update /etc/fstab lines
       that use those paths, and remount. Lines that use UUID= keep working.
       Never rename the VG that holds the root file system unless you also
       change the boot loader's kernel arguments.

EXAMPLES
           vgrename vgdata vgprojects

SEE ALSO
       lvrename(8), vgs(8), fstab(5)
